#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a real quantum processor, noise turns the pure state $|\\psi\\rangle$ "
"that a circuit is designed to prepare into a mixed state $\\rho$. Full "
"quantum state tomography can reconstruct $\\rho$, but the number of "
"measurements it needs grows exponentially with the number of qubits. Votto "
"et al. [\\[1\\]](#references) instead learned a compact model of $\\rho$ for"
" up to 96 qubits from randomized measurements. This tutorial follows their "
"workflow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In a randomized measurement [\\[2\\]](#references), every qubit $i$ is "
"rotated by an independent random unitary $u_i$ and then measured in the "
"computational basis. One draw of the rotations is called a *measurement "
"setting*, and each setting is repeated for $N_M$ shots. A shot with outcome "
"bits $s_i$ gives the *classical shadow* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"whose average over settings and shots is $\\rho$. The prerequisite tutorial "
"draws each $u_i$ from the three Pauli bases; this tutorial, like the paper, "
"draws them uniformly from all single-qubit unitaries (Haar random), and the "
"same formula applies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shadows estimate properties of a few qubits at a time. The paper combines "
"them into a *matrix product operator* (MPO), which writes the density matrix"
" as a chain of small tensors, one per qubit; noisy states with short-range "
"correlations need only small bonds between neighboring tensors. Like the "
"density matrix renormalization group (DMRG) algorithm, the learner sweeps "
"along the chain and updates one tensor at a time, so that the model matches "
"the shadows on the window of $2\\ell+1$ qubits centered on that tensor "
"(Equation 4 of the paper). The bond dimension stays fixed during these "
"updates, so the learner never truncates the model. Because data enter only "
"through these windows, the number of settings needed does not grow with the "
"length of the chain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The settings are split into a training set and a testing set. On the testing"
" set, the paper estimates the max fidelity between $\\rho$ and the model "
"$\\sigma$,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measuring $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ directly would take exponentially "
"many measurements. Instead, the paper assumes the *approximate factorization"
" condition* (AFC): correlations in $\\rho$ decay within a few qubits, so "
"global overlaps and purities factor into terms on blocks of $k$ neighboring "
"qubits. The purity also gives the Rényi-2 entropy "
"$S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, which measures how mixed the state "
"is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The paper prepares the depth-$D$ kicked-Ising state\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on 96 qubits of `ibm_brisbane`, an Eagle processor, with 2,048 settings of "
"1,024 shots for $D=1$. Figure 1(c,d) of the paper reports two results for "
"$D=1$:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learned model reaches $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ with the "
"experimental state at $N=96$, far above the overlap of the ideal state "
"$|\\psi\\rangle$ with the experiment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The entropy grows linearly, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ to }0.15)\\,N$, and the"
" entropy of the model agrees with an independent estimate from the testing "
"set.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial checks both results, first in an eight-qubit simulation where "
"the exact answers are known, and then in a new 96-qubit run on `ibm_fez`, a "
"Heron r2 processor. The learner is an independent Julia implementation of "
"the equations in the paper and its supplement.\n"
msgstr ""

